# What NOT to send to the daemon.
#
# The build context is tarred and uploaded before the first instruction runs, so everything here is time on every
# build and, for anything secret, a layer in the image if a COPY picks it up.
#
# The .git directory is the big one: on a repo with history it can be larger than the source, and nothing in a Go
# build needs it. The exception is a build that reads the commit with `go build -buildvcs`, which needs it and is
# why this repo passes the commit as a build ARG instead.

.git
.gitignore

# Anything a local run produced.
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
bin/
dist/

# The Dockerfiles themselves: changing one should not invalidate the build context of the others.
dockerfiles/
docker-compose.yml
README.md
*.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
